{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), so nearly all design dimensions remain unexplored. The most consequential architectural question is whether the image modality adds value at all. Config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is a minimal, clean extension of config_001: it keeps the exact same RNA pipeline and profile setting and adds only the image branch with the simplest standard fusion (concat). This lets us directly attribute any accuracy/F1 change to the inclusion of image features. If it improves over 48.5%, we gain strong evidence to invest further in multimodal configurations (encoder choice, fusion strategy, multiprofile). If it does not, we can rule out the image modality early and concentrate the remaining budget on RNA-only design choices (encoder, multiprofile, aggregation). Resnet50 is chosen over ViT-L as the more standard, lower-risk starting point. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the highest-impact design decision under a tight budget."
}

